WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.200
Put a single atom on the most
sensitive balance in the lab.

2
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.280
The display won't even flicker.

3
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:11.060
Yet chemists give boron an
average atomic mass of 10.8.

4
00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:13.860
And they know boron comes
in two kinds of atom,

5
00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.920
called isotopes, each with its own mass.

6
00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:21.780
So how can anyone weigh atoms that
are far too small for any balance?

7
00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.940
In this mission, you'll
read a mass spectrum:

8
00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:29.340
one peak for each isotope, and a
height that shows how common it is.

9
00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:34.900
Then you'll turn the peaks of a spectrum into
a single average mass for the whole element.

10
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:39.810
Your mission: find out how to weigh atoms
that no balance could ever detect.